1 NOTE CIO: one record shows, 24 Mar 1834 for birthdate. The cemetery record book in the Philipsburg Town Hall shows him as a confederate soldier. I have not checked on this yet. (still haven't as of June 1996). Have now,but no luck, will continue
2 CONC  off and on as more records become available.(2006)
2 CONT 
2 CONT  obituary in Philipsburg (MT) Mail, 1893 says he was born in Kentucky, moved to St. Louis at age 5-6. Need to check further on this. Hopefully this May/June 1994 in person. He was born in New York City per letters from Lucy Bakewell Audubon
2 CONC  to her relatives in England and also the 1850 St. Louis, Missouri census.
2 CONT 
2 CONT  The submission records were put in with the birthplace of St. Louis, Missouri as that is what all the family KNEW!
2 CONT 
2 CONT  With 28 years age difference between him and his wife....? I wonder if he was married before? Obituary says he was a Harvard man, (they have no record of him as an alumni but he could have attended there). He worked the river boats for yea
2 CONC rs except for a couple right after he and Susy were married and later worked as a bookkeeper for the mines in Philipsburg, MT. another riddle to solve.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Listed in MT 1890 Veterans Index pg 38, living in Philipsburg,Deer Lodge Co, MT (Granite county was formed from this)
